 SkinThickness, DiabetesPedigreeFunction) to normalize their distributions and improve model performance.\n\n3. **Removed problematic features**: Eliminated categorical features and interaction terms that either caused NaN issues or degraded performance.\n\n### Final Pipeline Features:\n- 12 total features (including the original 8 plus 4 engineered features)\n- No categorical variables that caused conversion issues\n- Carefully selected ratio and log-transformed features\n- Maintained the original model configuration\n\n### Performance Results:\n- Best score achieved: 1-auroc = 0.1653 (eval #7)\n- Baseline score: 1-auroc = 0.1670\n- This represents a 0.0017 improvement in the 1-auroc metric\n\nThe improvements were achieved through careful feature engineering focused on domain-relevant relationships while avoiding over-engineering that could lead to instability or poor generalization.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_655f5d8183c74d4cbc2e0458","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"pipeline.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":14155,"output":334,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14489,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790974312312,"responseId":"chatcmpl-90ae991f651bacad","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_655f5d8183c74d4cbc2e0458","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create domain-specific features\n    X_train = X_train.copy()\n    X_test = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Add glucose to BMI ratio\n    X_train['glucose_bmi_ratio'] = X_train['Glucose'] / (X_train['BMI'] + 1e